    "nombre": "Ed Watts",
    "foto": null,
    "biografia_limpia": "Ed Watts was a Hot Wheels employee who worked for Mattel from the 1980s to the early 2000s; he is known to have worked on Masters of the Universe figures as well as the Top Speed line of Hot Wheels cars. He retired in 2002 due to a stage 4 brain tumor diagnosis, with the Ed Watts Race Team Red Line Club set created to honor him; all the proceeds from the set would go to Watts's family. He unfortunately lost his battle with cancer some time later.",
    "bio_es": null,
    "bio_en": "Ed Watts was a Hot Wheels employee who worked for Mattel from the 1980s to the early 2000s; he is known to have worked on Masters of the Universe figures as well as the Top Speed line of Hot Wheels cars. He retired in 2002 due to a stage 4 brain tumor diagnosis, with the Ed Watts Race Team Red Line Club set created to honor him; all the proceeds from the set would go to Watts's family. He unfortunately lost his battle with cancer some time later.",
